>Why is there all this guaranteed junk in Vlad's tower? Except for the
>amulet of life saving, and perhaps the water walking boots for those
>unlucky chaps who fall past Medusa, the guaranteed items are
>superseeded by the time you get there. Does anybody know bits of an
>explanation or perhaps the history of this stuff?

In 3.0.x, Vlad's Tower was located inside Hell (which rather different from the
modern Gehennom; see http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Hell).  The first level of
the Tower was directly connected to the maze on its level; the others were
isolated, much as the Wizard's Tower is now.

The Wizard had the Amulet, and there were no invocation artifacts nor a Sanctum.
Thus Vlad's Tower was strictly optional.  The loot therein might prove useful to
some players.  This loot was the same as today, except that Vlad had no
candelabrum.



